        brief: `Nested \`x-data\` elements create nested scopes. Reading walks **outwards** until a scope has the property; writing always writes to the **nearest** scope that owns it \u2014 creating the property in the inner scope if it does not exist anywhere.

So a child that assigns to a name the parent owns will change the parent (any name it can see), but a child that declares the same name in its own \`x-data\` **shadows** it and the parent never notices.`,
