    goal: "Choose deliberately between hiding an element and removing it \u2014 and be able to explain the state consequences of each.",
    intro: `Two directives, one decision. **\`x-show\`** flips \`display: none\`; the element (and its state, focus, inputs, children) stays right where it is. **\`x-if\`** adds and removes the element entirely, so anything living inside it is destroyed and rebuilt.

The cost is the other way round: \`x-show\` is cheap to toggle but the element is always in the DOM, and \`x-if\` costs a teardown/rebuild every time it flips but keeps the DOM clean and the memory small.`,
