        scenario: `An underwriter types a mortality loading and a retention limit. The form must survive a page reload: every change mirrors the draft into \`localStorage\` under the key \`${KEY}\`, and on boot the component restores whatever is there. A \`data-testid="saved"\` counter shows how many times the draft has been mirrored, and \`data-testid="restored"\` reads \`yes\` when a stored draft was found.

This is what the persist plugin does for you in module 12 \u2014 here you build it by hand so that the plugin is not magic later.`,
        brief: `Elements: \`data-testid="loading"\` (number, %), \`data-testid="retention"\` (number), \`data-testid="saved"\` (effect run count), \`data-testid="restored"\` (\`yes\`/\`no\`), \`data-testid="clear"\` (wipes the stored draft and resets the fields). Storage key: \`${KEY}\`.`,
        starter: `<div x-data="{ loading: 0, retention: 1000000 }">
</div>`,
