        brief: `Register an \`Alpine.bind('sumField', () => ({ \u2026 }))\` bundle that sets \`type="number"\`, \`step="10000"\`, an \`:id\` and \`:aria-describedby\` from \`$id\`-style static ids (\`sum-input\` / \`sum-hint\`), an \`:class\` that adds \`touched\` once \`touches > 0\`, and \`@input\` that counts edits and stores the numeric value in \`sum\`. The component itself (\`x-data\`) holds \`sum\`, \`touches\` and a \`reset()\`, and the page shows \`data-testid="sum"\`, \`data-testid="touches"\`, \`data-testid="reset"\` and a \`data-testid="hint"\` paragraph with \`id="sum-hint"\`.`,
